# Authored content. Never in the repo: a public repo publishes every future
# day in plaintext, and git history keeps it there. Content lives in the
# database and is served through the date gate in /api/puzzle.
# `content/*` rather than `content/`: a negation cannot reach inside an
# excluded directory, so the directory itself has to stay visible for the
# sample below to be re-included.
content/*
puzzles/
public/puzzles/
# The development sample is invented placeholder content, committed so a fresh
# clone can play without a database. It is not scheduled and reveals nothing
# about the real queue.
!content/sample.json
.vercel

# Never in a public repo. `vercel env pull` writes the database URL here.
.env*
